From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:28:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: reset QCA8386 after PHY package setup

MHT has a switch-core reset independent of its PHY and PCS resets.
QSDK R48 configures SRAM timing, PCS1 and clock sources before resetting
that core and MAC0-5 TX/RX, then programs switch forwarding. Resetting
the core at probe, before phylink initializes the shared PHY package,
leaves QM running across those package changes. Rebinding after package
initialization drains a reproduced stuck queue without a system reboot.

Initialize the shared package through its first PHY, then pulse the
optional ordered NSSCC reset array at the start of DSA setup. Correct
the core reset register from 0xc to CBCR 0x8 bit 2 and use R48's 10us
pulse. Leave other QCA8K families and old device trees unchanged. This
is one-time initialization, not a running-switch recovery mechanism.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Signed-off-by: lean <chenlin@fnnas.com>

---

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/dsa/qca8k.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/dsa/qca8k.yaml
@@ -45,6 +45,14 @@
       GPIO to be used to reset the whole device
     maxItems: 1
 
+  resets:
+    description:
+      QCA8386 NSSCC resets, ordered as switch core then MAC0 through MAC5,
+      each with TX followed by RX. Reset the core after its clocks are
+      available and before configuring DSA forwarding.
+    minItems: 13
+    maxItems: 13
+
   qca,ignore-power-on-sel:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/flag
     description:
